Fix two bugs in how UMR (d1cdaed) picks between its forward and backward solves.

Apply in the clone of UMR with `git apply selection.patch`. Two solver keys of the batch
config switch the fixes, and each default keeps the behavior of UMR:

  trajectory_warm_start_bidirectional_continuity_space: "joints" (UMR) or "qpos".
      "qpos" also charges a jump of the root between the two solves: the whole
      configuration by mj_differentiatePos, root in m and rad, joints in rad, weight 1.
  frame_cost_at_solution: false (UMR) or true.
      UMR compares each frame by its residual before the last solver step, which with
      one step per frame is the residual of the start pose. true adds one residual pass
      at the returned pose, without a step, and compares that.

warm_start_debug_dir saves both solves, both costs, and the pick of each frame.

The sequential solve of umr/batch.json is bit-identical with or without the patch.
See "Why UMR slides" in docs/comparison.md for what the fixes change.

